              the effects of estrogen are mediated through two functionally distinct receptors , estrogen receptor 

              ( er- 
               ) , and estrogen receptor 

              ( er- 
              ) , both of which are expressed in the cardiovascular system . 
the etiology of cardiovascular disease is believed to result in part from the loss of endogenous estrogen , indicating that estrogen and its receptors may play important roles in the prevention of cardiovascular disease in women .
